    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="c5f8b45e-eeb0-5701-ac7e-c1ba49d41d1d" activityNameId="b31ab750-995d-545e-8f9a-e5bf38b3af0c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Asphalt concrete (AC) surface layer, 0% recycling, high temperature, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Asphalt concrete (AC) surface layer, 0% recycling, high temperature, at plant
Modern Swiss technologies for regional storage facilities, material extraction, and asphalt production. Based on survey data from 73 asphalt mixing plants. 
UUID: 722099bb-168b-4ffe-a530-6bd14ad3805a
This dataset covers the production of average Asphalt Concrete (AC) surface layers in Switzerland, with 0% reclaimed asphalt. The process represents an average AC, derived from the mean material composition of multiple AC L, AC H, AC N and AC S layers. It includes raw material extraction, transportation, and manufacturing processes.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: Production of hot mix asphalt concrete AC, using industrial machinery.
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 351352456 t 
Sampling: Survey
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_722099bb-168b-4ffe-a530-6bd14ad3805a.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
